        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Persian Constitutional Revolution</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>): <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rasht">Rasht</a>, Qazvin, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a> and other cities, with the Shi'i schools of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najaf">Najaf</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> giving rulings from outside.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Protest against the customs director and the shah's loans (1905); the shah's agreement to a house of justice (January 1906) and to a parliament (August 1906); the first Majlis (from October 1906); the Minor Tyranny and civil war (1908–1909); the second constitutional period (1909–1911); the expulsion of the deputies of the Second Majlis (December 1911).</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Leading figures</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozaffar-ad-din-shah-qajar">Mozaffar ad-Din Shah Qajar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-ali-shah-qajar">Mohammad Ali Shah Qajar</a>; the clerics Akhund Khurasani, Mirza Husayn Tehrani, Shaykh Abdullah Mazandarani, Sayyed Mohammad Tabatabai and Fazlollah Nouri; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> commanders <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sattar-khan">Sattar Khan</a> and Bagher Khan; Yeprem Khan; the American lawyer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morgan-shuster">William Morgan Shuster</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">A parliament with final approval of loans and the budget, and a constitution that lasted, though not adhered to, until 1979; but also the Anglo-Russian division of the country in 1907, the shelling of the Majlis in 1908, and the expulsion of the Second Majlis in 1911 with the support of 12,000 Russian troops.</span></div>
        </div>
